From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:19:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm6450: Use retention for USB power domain
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The USB controller does not expect to lose its state when it is
runtime suspended. With the power domain switched off, the QSCRATCH
glue registers go back to their reset values: on the Sony Xperia 10 VI,
GENERAL_CFG read 0x4 after a runtime suspend and resume instead of 0xd,
so the selection of the UTMI clock as the PIPE clock, which dwc3-qcom
makes only at probe, was gone, and the controller then failed to enable
its control endpoint:

  dwc3 a600000.usb: failed to enable ep0out

To keep the controller's state, the USB GDSC needs to stay in
retention, as it does on other similar SoCs. Change its mode to
PWRSTS_RET_ON.

To be folded into "clk: qcom: Add Global Clock Controller driver for SM6450"
once a round has run the controller through a runtime suspend with it.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6450.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6450.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6450.c
index fe41abb57..4b78b03eb 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6450.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6450.c
@@ -2504,7 +2504,7 @@ static struct gdsc gcc_usb30_prim_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "gcc_usb30_prim_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 };
 
